        {
          "_type": "UMLPackage",
          "_id": "c4-pkg-1366",
          "_parent": {
            "$ref": "c4-model-0002"
          },
          "name": "3.2 — Components · Driver",
          "documentation": "Inside driver.mjs. Two of these are shared modules the other stages import as well; they are drawn here because this is where they are first used.",
          "ownedElements": [
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-1367",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-1366"
              },
              "name": "Input resolver",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: driver.mjs\n\nReads argv. Anything not ending .mjs/.js is treated as a script and compiled; a target comes from --target, DEMO_TARGET, or a TARGET export on the scenario."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-1368",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-1366"
              },
              "name": "Script compiler",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: script.mjs · shared\n\nParses the .demo grammar — header directives, a selectors block, then beats — and emits a scenario module. The generated file is inspectable and hand-editable, so the script is a starting point rather than a black box."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-1369",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-1366"
              },
              "name": "Target loader",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: target.mjs · shared\n\nDeep-merges the target JSON, its .local.json sidecar, .env and the DEMO_* env vars, later winning, and resolves env:VAR_NAME values at load time. The one place credentials are allowed to appear."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-1370",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-1366"
              },
              "name": "Chrome launcher",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: puppeteer-core\n\nRuns a real Chrome on the target's profile (profile/ unless the target names another), pinned to --force-device-scale-factor=1 so display scaling cannot change the frame size. On macOS keeps --use-mock-keychain so profile cookies decrypt."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-1371",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-1366"
              },
              "name": "Sign-in step",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: driver.mjs\n\nFills the target's auth.selectors and waits the app out. auth.start decides whether the take opens signed-out, with the login part of the demo, or signed-in, with the login happening off-camera before capture starts."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-1372",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-1366"
              },
              "name": "Flow primitives",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: driver.mjs · d.*\n\nhold, waitSel, waitGone, appears, hoverSel, clickSel, type, key, wheel, open, race, login, logout. d.type verifies the click actually focused the element and refuses to type into the wrong one rather than sending text to whatever has focus. Click and hover scroll an off-screen element into view first; open fills {name} placeholders from the target's secrets."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-1373",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-1366"
              },
              "name": "Screencast recorder",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: CDP Page.startScreencast\n\nAcks every frame and writes out/frames/*.jpg plus frames.json. Gated on the take, so an off-camera sign-in never reaches the video."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-1374",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-1366"
              },
              "name": "Input telemetry recorder",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: driver.mjs\n\nSamples synthesized pointer moves and clicks into actions.json. The cursor in the finished video is drawn from this, which is why the capture needs no real cursor."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-1375",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-1366"
              },
              "name": "Narration cue collector",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: driver.mjs · d.say()\n\nStamps { t, text } at wall-clock time and returns immediately — the voice plays over the visuals instead of the flow pausing for it. Cue times are recorded during the take precisely because beat length varies per run."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-1376",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-1366"
              },
              "name": "Teardown",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: driver.mjs\n\nStops the screencast, writes frames.json and actions.json, and closes Chrome by its window rather than killing it, so unflushed session state is not lost."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-1377",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-1366"
              },
              "name": "Page conditioner",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: CDP Network.setBlockedURLs + injected CSS\n\nApplies the target to the page before the take: blockUrls keeps third-party widgets such as a chat bubble from loading, and hideSelectors hides app banners on this page and every page loaded after it."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-1378",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-1366"
              },
              "name": "Wait logger",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: driver.mjs · timed()\n\nTimes every open, wait and wait-gone the flow makes, keeping { start, end, kind, spec }. Written to actions.json for the assembler to fast-forward the long ones."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClassDiagram",
              "_id": "c4-dgm-1379",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-1366"
              },
              "name": "C4-L3 — Components · Driver (driver.mjs)",
              "documentation": "Level 3, container \"2 · Driver\".",
              "defaultDiagram": false,
              "ownedViews": [
                {
                  "_type": "UMLClassView",
                  "_id": "c4-v-1380",
