        {
          "_type": "UMLPackage",
          "_id": "c4-pkg-1999",
          "_parent": {
            "$ref": "c4-model-0002"
          },
          "name": "3.5 — Components · Compositor",
          "documentation": "Inside compose.mjs. Replaces the macOS-only Recordly step by rendering every frame itself. Frames stream in from ffmpeg and straight back out to it, so nothing intermediate hits disk.",
          "ownedElements": [
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-2000",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-1999"
              },
              "name": "Project reader",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: compose.mjs\n\nReads {take}.recordly and the take it names, so the composite is always of the video the project was built from."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-2001",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-1999"
              },
              "name": "Look resolver",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: compose.mjs + brand.mjs\n\npadding, radius, shadow, background, ramp and pan timings, from the project frame block and overridable by NO_FRAME and PADDING. The mat the window sits on is the brand blue: it is most of what the viewer sees for the length of the demo, so either it carries the brand colour or the video does not have one."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-2002",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-1999"
              },
              "name": "Probe",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: ffprobe\n\nDimensions, frame rate and frame count of the take."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-2003",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-1999"
              },
              "name": "Cursor track",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: compose.mjs\n\nSplits telemetry into moves and clicks, then works out when the cursor actually left one point and settled on the next. A held zoom that jumps between click positions would otherwise leave the cursor off screen while it travels."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-2004",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-1999"
              },
              "name": "Zoom keyframe track",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: compose.mjs\n\nFour keyframes per region — ramp up, hold, hold, ramp down — interpolated with an ease-in-out cubic. Between regions the track sits at zoom 1, where focus is irrelevant, so interpolating across the gap is safe."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-2005",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-1999"
              },
              "name": "Cursor sprites",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: @napi-rs/canvas\n\nArrow and pointing hand drawn once into sprites, then composited with a press scale and a click ripple. This is why the capture needs no real cursor."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-2006",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-1999"
              },
              "name": "Frame renderer",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: @napi-rs/canvas\n\nPer frame: the source into its own canvas, the zoom transform clipped to the rounded window, the shadow, then the cursor on top."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-2007",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-1999"
              },
              "name": "Decoder pipe",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: ffmpeg rawvideo rgba\n\nStreams the take in. The decoder delivers small pipe chunks, which are reassembled into one reused frame buffer rather than a freshly concatenated one per frame."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-2008",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-1999"
              },
              "name": "Encoder pipe",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: ffmpeg libx264\n\nTakes rendered frames straight back, with faststart. Backpressure is respected by waiting on drain rather than buffering the whole video."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClassDiagram",
              "_id": "c4-dgm-2009",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-1999"
              },
