        {
          "_type": "UMLPackage",
          "_id": "c4-pkg-2809",
          "_parent": {
            "$ref": "c4-model-0002"
          },
          "name": "3.9 — Components · Quality Gate",
          "documentation": "Inside qa.mjs. Per-line checks run where cue times are still the take's own timeline — the narrated video; whole-video checks run on the deliverable. It reports; it never fixes.",
          "ownedElements": [
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-2810",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-2809"
              },
              "name": "Input resolver",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: qa.mjs\n\nThe deliverable (the newest stage output, or --video), the narrated video, the cue file the narrator used, and the intro and outro card lengths to leave out of the whole-video checks."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-2811",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-2809"
              },
              "name": "Lineage check",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: qa.mjs · file times\n\nEvery stage output the deliverable is built from must be newer than the one before it. A stage that did not write leaves an older take's file behind and the next stage joins it: a clean-looking video of the wrong take."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-2812",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-2809"
              },
              "name": "Stream check",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: ffprobe\n\nAudio and video of the same length and with the same start, or the whole track is shifted."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-2813",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-2809"
              },
              "name": "Line checker",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: qa.mjs + TTS clip cache\n\nOverlap: a line still speaking when the next starts — two voices at once. Sync: every line has to start within 250ms of its cue in the narrated video. Line lengths come from the clip cache, so it never calls the TTS API."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-2814",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-2809"
              },
              "name": "Dead-air detector",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: ffmpeg silencedetect\n\n4s without narration warns and 6s fails, outside the title cards."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-2815",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-2809"
              },
              "name": "Freeze classifier",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: ffmpeg freezedetect\n\nA still picture with the voice over most of it is a deliberate hold and only warns; a still picture in silence is a wait and fails at 5s. Pauses under 0.8s count as speech, or the gaps between the clauses of one line would score a correctly paced hold as silent."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-2816",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-2809"
              },
              "name": "Black and loudness",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: ffmpeg blackdetect + ebur128\n\nBlack frames fail. Integrated loudness outside -19..-13 LUFS, or a true peak above -1 dBFS, warns."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-2817",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-2809"
              },
              "name": "Still extractor",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: ffmpeg\n\nOne still mid-line for every narration line and one for every flagged range: what the visual review looks at."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-2818",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-2809"
              },
              "name": "Report writer",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: qa.json\n\nThe verdict, findings ordered fail-first, every line with its timing and still. Exits 1 on any failure, so it can end a build."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClassDiagram",
