        {
          "_type": "UMLPackage",
          "_id": "c4-pkg-3351",
          "_parent": {
            "$ref": "c4-model-0002"
          },
          "name": "3.11 — Components · Memory",
          "documentation": "Inside memory.mjs. Bookkeeping for project memory: it never reads an online source itself (only the memory agent can, through MCP tools), but it decides what changed, merges what the agent found, and keeps Zep in step with the repo.",
          "ownedElements": [
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-3352",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-3351"
              },
              "name": "Source resolver",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: sources.json + .env · source\n\nFinds the apps (one folder per app under memory/features), the catalog of each, and its online source from FEATURE_SOURCE_{APP} in .env; recognises the kind of source and names the tools to list and read it."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-3353",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-3351"
              },
              "name": "Change detector",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: diff · baseline\n\nCompares a source listing with the sync lock: new, changed, removed, unchanged. Files dated on or before the catalog generated date are its baseline, recorded without being read."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-3354",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-3351"
              },
              "name": "Catalog merger",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: upsert\n\nMerges the features the agent found into data/features.json: matched by name, a new one gets the next feature id; totals and the updated date follow."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-3355",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-3351"
              },
              "name": "Sync lock",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: mark · synced\n\ndata/sources.lock.json next to each catalog: every source file seen, its kind and the features it fed, and when the app was last synced. Private with its app."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-3356",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-3351"
              },
              "name": "Staleness check",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: staleSources() · MEMORY_MAX_AGE_H\n\nApps whose source was last synced longer ago than the limit. Read by the session hook and by build.mjs."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-3357",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-3351"
              },
              "name": "Session hook",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: hook · SessionStart\n\nRuns when a Claude Code session starts: attributes the session to its user, opens its Zep thread, and asks Claude to launch the memory agent when a source is stale."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-3358",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-3351"
              },
              "name": "Session attribution",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: MEMORY_USER · Zep users and threads\n\nOne Zep user per person (MEMORY_USER, else git user.email) and one thread per Claude session; zep session adds notes to it."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-3359",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-3351"
              },
              "name": "Video state",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: video state · video review · video accept · video sync\n\nOne state file per video next to its page: status (not built, build failed, qa failed, awaiting review, review failed, done, accepted, published), last build with qa counts, the visual review, the user's acceptance of a build with open findings (never recorded as a PASS) and a history. Generates the Video status section of the page, sends the state to the app graph and posts the whole status to the video thread."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-3360",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-3351"
              },
              "name": "Session recorder",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: session flush (Stop) · session end (SessionEnd) · session video\n\nAfter every Claude turn, and at the end, pushes what the person typed and Claude answered from the transcript, tool output left out and emails and phone numbers masked, then a summary built from the record: prompts, files changed, commits, pull requests. Each new video starts a new thread, so a video is a session of its own."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-3361",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-3351"
              },
              "name": "Zep publisher",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: zep push\n\nTurns catalogs (one document per feature), video pages, rules, pipeline lessons, flows, traces and manifests (not generated scripts or videos) into Zep documents in the graph of their app. Sends only what changed; a full push removes documents whose file is gone."
            },
            {
              "_type": "UMLClass",
              "_id": "c4-el-3362",
              "_parent": {
                "$ref": "c4-pkg-3351"
              },
              "name": "Zep search",
              "stereotype": {
                "$ref": "c4-st-0009"
              },
              "documentation": "Technology: zep search\n\nFacts from the graph of one app, or of all of them."
            },
            {
